# dynep: Python SDK for Real-Time Cloud GPU Spot Intelligence

[![PyPI Version](https://img.shields.io/pypi/v/dynep.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/dynep/)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-emerald.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
[![Endpoint](https://img.shields.io/badge/API-data.dynep.com-blue)](https://data.dynep.com)

The official Python client for **[Dynep](https://data.dynep.com)** — the autonomous real-time cloud GPU spot market indexer tracking 31 cloud providers (RunPod, Lambda Labs, Vast.ai, LeaderGPU, AWS, Vultr, FluidStack, and more).

Stop overpaying for fine-tuning and inference compute. Find the lowest hourly spot rate for NVIDIA H100, H200, B200, A100, and RTX 4090 in milliseconds.

---

## ⚡ Installation

```bash
pip install dynep
```

---

## 🚀 Quickstart (Zero-Auth)

Query real-time spot rates across 31 providers instantly without registering or needing an API key:

```python
from dynep import DynepClient

client = DynepClient()

# 1. Fetch live market spot benchmark summary across all GPU families
quotes = client.get_spot_summary()

for q in quotes:
    print(f"{q.gpu_model}: ${q.spot_rate_hourly_usd}/hr on {q.best_provider} (Savings vs AWS: {q.cost_savings_vs_aws_percent})")

# 2. Find the single cheapest spot instance for a specific GPU model
best_h100 = client.get_cheapest_spot("H100")
if best_h100:
    print(f"\nCheapest H100: ${best_h100.spot_rate_hourly_usd}/hr via {best_h100.best_provider}")
    print(f"AWS equivalent: ${best_h100.aws_equivalent_rate_usd}/hr")
```

---

## 🔑 Claim Complimentary Developer API Key (100 reqs/mo)

You can claim an instant evaluation API key programmatically:

```python
from dynep import DynepClient

res = DynepClient.claim_free_key("developer@startup.ai")
print(f"Your API Key: {res['api_key']}")
print(f"Monthly Quota: {res['monthly_quota']} requests")
```

---

## 📊 Full Structured Feed Queries (With API Key)

Query paginated, filtered hardware instance feeds with region, VRAM, and provider metadata:

```python
from dynep import DynepClient

client = DynepClient(api_key="sk_live_your_api_key_here")

# Filter instances by GPU model
results = client.query_live_instances(search="H100", limit=10)

for record in results.get("data", []):
    item = record["data"]
    print(f"[{item.get('provider')}] {item.get('title')} - ${item.get('price')}/hr ({item.get('category')})")
```

